 "_doc": "LR-139: the parts of the 2D pawns as data. tools/game_2d/native/pixels2d.cpp and web/pawns.js only stamp them, so a new cut, beard, ear or build needs no rebuild (restart the window). An op = {shapes | one shape's fields, colour, outline (true), flat (set pixels as they are), pattern {if, colour}, sides 'SEN' (W mirrors E)}. A shape = {ell: [cx, cy, rx, ry]} | {head: true} | {body: true} | {px: [[x, y]...]} | '@name' (shapes below), with sides, when (the whole shape), where (each pixel), minus (a shape). Numbers may be expressions over x y (the pixel), hcx hcy hrx hry (head centre, radii), top (the head's top row), fx fy (face column and eye row), ey (the head's middle row), hl hrr (the head's left and right columns), eb (the back of the head seen from the east), nx (the nose tip column from the east), bcx bcy brx bry bx by (the body), step swing child; with + - * / % < <= > >= == != && || ! abs min max trunc floor. Colours: skin, hair, eye, hat, c (the op's own), the names in colours, '#hex', 'name*0.8', 'mix(a,b,0.45)'. Shapes also: {rect: [x0, y0, x1, y1]}, {col: [x, y0, y1]} (a stick). Groups are drawn in this order: hair.back (behind the body), cloak.back, the body (+ skin_patterns.body), feet (colour feet: the boots' if worn), wear (each worn layer, colour wear), cloak.front, hands, tools (tx ty: by the tool hand; hy, sw: the hands' swing; footy), ears (under the head and again over the hair unless the cut is in bald), head (+ skin_patterns.head), face, brows, noses, beards, tusks, hair.front, hats. The species (content/species/*.json body.pawn) name the entries: ears, head, nose, brow, eyes, tusks, build, skin_pattern; hair_m / hair_f / beards are the kind's sets.",
